tion\": \"Which of the user's accounts to use.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"checking\",\n            \"savings\"\n          ],\n          \"default\": \"checking\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": []\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"updateUserRole\",\n    \"description\": \"Change the role of one user account, which sets what the user can see and edit in the workspace.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"userId\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"Numeric user id, e.g. 48213.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"New role for the account.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"viewer\",\n            \"editor\",\n            \"admin\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"notifyUser\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"description\": \"Email the user about the change.\",\n          \"default\": true\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"userId\",\n        \"role\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: Find the users named Okafor.\n\nReply with only a JSON array of the tool calls that fulfil the request, each of the form {\"name\": \"<tool name>\", \"arguments\": {...}}, where \"arguments\" is a JSON object (not a string). When the request needs several calls, list them all. Reply with [] if no tool fits the request, or if the request does not give a value for a required argument: never guess one. Include every required argument. Include an optional argument only if the request asks for a value for it; otherwise leave it out and the tool applies its default. Give each value the type its schema declares: JSON numbers for integer and number, true or false for boolean, and strings for string, copied exactly as written.","role":"user"},{"content":"[{\"name\":\"searchUsers\",\"arguments\":{\"query\":\"Okafor\"}}]","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool results:\n[\n  {\n    \"na